# --- Dynamic provider GROUPS: merge multiple [dynamic_providers.<name>]
# entries into ONE combined output, real repo. cli/sdk.go's own
# generateDynamicProviderGroup/mergeDynamicProviderGroupMembers -- fetches
# every listed member independently, unions their Resources/DataSources/
# signals/describe_exclude (a real collision across members fails loud,
# never silently picks one), and calls writeGeneratedSDK ONCE with
# shortName = repo_name (falling back to this table's own key if unset).
#
# Table key vs repo_name, real bug this file's own first live run caught:
# this table was originally keyed "google" too, identically to the
# standalone [dynamic_providers.google] Compute-only entry above --
# `--only google` matched BOTH in the same run, both writing to the same
# output path (the second write silently landing on top of the first).
# Keyed "google_all" instead (distinct from every real
# [dynamic_providers.<name>] entry, so `--only google_all` can never
# collide with a standalone target), with repo_name = "google" carrying
# the real published repo identity separately -- see
# generateDynamicProviderGroup's own doc comment (cli/sdk.go) for the
# full account, including a second, related bug this same run caught
# (source driving the output DIRECTORY name too, via
# sanitizeSourceForFilename -- fixed by setting source = repoName
# verbatim, not a decorated description).
#
# `ubx sdk gen --only google_all --out .` generates the group under the
# real "google" repo identity -- `--only google` still means the bare
# Compute-only entry above, `--only google_dataflow` (etc.) still
# generates that ONE member standalone, unaffected; a group is purely
# additive.
#
# [dynamic_provider_groups.google_all]: every real GCP Discovery Doc
# entry above (the original google/compute entry plus all 161
# google_<api> entries), merged into the single, real, published
# github.com/ubiquex/ubx-sdk-google identity -- the real fix for the gap
# the google_<api> block's own NAMING CAVEAT comment named ("no such
# repo exists or is planned" is no longer true; this table is that
# repo's real, full source list).

